-- title:
--   Equivariant archimedean cut projectors transport right convolutions
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let `tys : ArchTypeFamily F` be a family assigning to each infinite place $w$ of $F$ a number `tys.card w` of representations `tys.rep w i` of the group `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ w.Completion` on finite-dimensional complex spaces; write $A$ for `archCutSubmodule F tys`, the intersection over all infinite places $w$ of the sum over $i$ of the type submodules `typeSubmodule (rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w) (tys.rep w i)` inside the space of functions $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$. Let $Q$ be any $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of that function space such that: (1) $Q\varphi=\varphi$ for every continuous $\varphi\in A$; (2) whenever $\varphi$ is continuous and the span of the right translates `rightTranslate F k φ`, $x\mapsto\varphi(xk)$, by elements $k$ of the subgroup $\bigsqcup_w$ generated by the ranges of the maps `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` is finite-dimensional, $Q\varphi$ lies in the intersection of $A$ with that span; (3) for such $\varphi$, $Q$ commutes with right translation by each such $k$. Let $y$ be continuous with $y\in A$, let `tys'` be a further type family, and let $f$ be a factorizable test function (a product of a compactly supported factor smooth in the archimedean matrix entries with a locally constant compactly supported factor at the finite places) which is `IsArchBiFinite F tys' f`, i.e. $x\mapsto f(x^{-1})$ lies in `archCutSubmodule F tys'` and $f$ lies in `archDualCutSubmodule F tys'`. Then there is a factorizable test function $f'$ with `IsArchBiFinite F tys f'` and $Q(y*f)=y*f'$, where $y*h$ denotes `rightConv F y h`, the function $g\mapsto\int y(gx)h(x)\,dx$ against the Haar measure on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$. Note that the output is bi-finite for `tys`, not for `tys'`.
--
--   This is the transport step for the archimedean $K$-type cut: an abstract projector onto a prescribed family of archimedean types, equivariant for right translation by the archimedean row-isometry subgroups, moves the cut from the automorphic side to the test-function side of a right convolution. It is used in the construction of such a projector, [`AutomorphicForm.exists_linearMap_archCutProjector`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_linearMap_archCutProjector).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector.lean

